# The panel's controls, clicked (scripts\verify\panel.ps1, part clicks), live:
#   RayTracingViewer cornell -w 1280 --height 720 -s 32 --input tests\window-panel-clicks.input --record r.txt
# tests\window-panel-asked.input asks for the same by actions, at the same frames; the two recordings must hold the
# same settings in the same order and end on the same frame, and the two saves must be the same bytes. A click is
# three events (the mouse moves to the control's middle, presses, lets go), which the panel takes over two frames.
at 0 action panel on
# The scene list: checker, a book scene in sight in the list's box
at 20 click scene checker
# The strategy's box opened, then material in it
at 50 click sampling
at 55 click sampling material
# The tone map's box, agx; the exposure up twice
at 80 click tonemap
at 85 click tonemap agx
at 110 click exposure up
at 120 click exposure up
# Twice the samples; the lens's slider is left alone, which must change nothing
at 140 click samples twice
# Saved once the image is done
at 260 click save
at 280 quit
